<main class="main-content">
    <h1>Commands</h1>
    <p>A detailed list of OnlyOneMessage's commands, what it does, its restrictions, and its parameters.</p>

    <div class="hint-card hint">
        <div class="icon">💡</div>
        <p>
            OnlyOneMessage uses a simple and intuitive command system to provide a seamless experience for administrators. 
            There is <b>no web-dashboard</b> for this bot... yet!
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>/addchannel</h2>
    <p>Add a channel for OnlyOneMessage to manage. A blacklist role will be created for the channel, allowing OnlyOneMessage to control cooldowns.</p>
    <p>Required Permissions: <b><code>Manage Roles</code>, <code>Manage Channels</code> & <code>Manage Threads</code></b></p>

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Parameter</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Description</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>channel</code></td>
                <td>Text Channel</td>
                <td>The channel where OnlyOneMessage will manage messages.</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
                <td><code>duration</code></td>
                <td>Select</td>
                <td>How long the blacklist role will be applied for, up to forever.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="hint-card hint">
        <div class="icon">💡</div>
        <p>
            You can add as many channels as you want, and each one can have a different duration.
            If a channel already has a built-in cooldown applied, the bot will remove it.
        </p>
    </div>


    <h2>/removechannel</h2>
    <p>
        Removes a specified channel from OnlyOneMessage's configuration.
        The created blacklist role <b>will be deleted</b>, but the channel will not. <i>(Originally did pre-v2.0).</i>
    </p>

    <p>Required Permissions: <b><code>Manage Roles</code>, <code>Manage Channels</code></b></p>

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Parameter</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Description</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>channel</code></td>
                <td>Text Channel</td>
                <td>The channel to remove configurations from.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>


    <h2>/config</h2>
    <p>
        Customize OnlyOneMessage's behavior for the server.
        Changed settings will apply to the whole server.
    </p>

    <p>Required Permissions: <b><code>Manage Roles</code>, <code>Manage Channels</code></b></p>

    <p>Categories:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><code>Logging</code> - Allow logging of bot & member actions.</li>
        <li><code>Bot Configuration</code> - Basic management options for the bot.</li>
    </ul>


    <h2>/configchannel</h2>
    <p>
        Customize OnlyOneMessage's behavior for a specific channel. 
        Changed settings will only apply to the specified channel.
    </p>
    <p>Required Permissions: <b><code>Manage Roles</code>, <code>Manage Channels</code></b></p>

    <p>Categories:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><code>Message Options</code> - Options for managing message behavior. These include cooldowns, message recovery & reactions.</li>
    </ul>

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Parameter</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Description</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>channel</code></td>
                <td>Text Channel</td>
                <td>The channel to modify configurations for.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    
    <h2>/invite</h2>
    <p>Sends an invite link to add OnlyOneMessage to your own server. That's pretty much all to say.</p>

    <h2>/feedback</h2>
    <p>
        Opens a Discord <code>Modal</code> to submit feedback to the OnlyOneMessage developers.
        Please note that this is for feedback regarding the bot and not for support inquiries. 
    </p>

    <h2>/stats</h2>
    <p>View basic statistics about OnlyOneMessage. This also includes individual server stats for blacklists and whitelists.</p>

    <div class="hint-card hint">
        <div class="icon">📰</div>
        <p>These statistics are also available under our <b>API Reference</b>.</p>
    </div>
</main>
